---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navigation from "../components/Navigation.astro";

---

<Layout
	title="Khora — Empirical Software Engineering Research Group"
	description="Khora research group in empirical software engineering at IRISA, Rennes."
>
	<Navigation />

	<main>
		<section class="main">
			<div class="main-content">
				<h1 class="team-name">Khora</h1>
				<p class="eyebrow">IRISA · Rennes, France</p>
				<p class="main-text-light">
					Research group in empirical software engineering at the IRISA laboratory, Rennes, France.
				</p>

				<p class="main-text">
					Software developers now have to explore and operate within an increasingly complex and constantly
					evolving design space, while having to deal with deploying new software releases faster. Khora is
					developing a research activity in software engineering to help developers in mastering their
					increasingly complex design space. To do so, Khora develops new scientific theories, approaches,
					and techniques related to exploratory programming, a development mode to try out, compare, explore
					different versions of software artifacts. Khora's research agenda implies working on:
					1. domain-specific IDEs and digital twins to help developers master their development design space
					through novel exploratory programming features (augmented development environment);
					2. large-scale, polyglot, AI-based, code analysis techniques to underpin exploratory programming
					(augmented code analysis). The application domains of Khora encompass software engineering with
					software artifacts (co-)evolution and optimization (e.g., reduce software energy consumption) and
					scientific computing to help scientists in their complex software development.
				</p>

				<p class="main-text">
					Khora is a research group part of the IRISA laboratory (a mixed research unit grouping CNRS,
					University of Rennes, Inria, INSA Rennes), Rennes, France.<br/>
					Khora is one of the spin-offs that succeeded <a href="//www.diverse-team.fr">DiverSE</a> in sept 2026
					(which itself succeeded <a href="//triskell.irisa.fr">Triskell</a> in 2013).
				</p>
				<div class="keywords">
					<span><a href="//www.irisa.fr/en/equipes/khora">IRISA</a></span>
					<span>CNRS</span>
					<span>University of Rennes</span>
					<span>Inria</span>
					<span>INSA Rennes</span>
				</div>
			</div>


		</section>

		<section class="section-divider main">
			<p class="main-text-light">
				Research Axes
			</p>

			<div class="main-content">
				<p class="main-text">Exploratory programming requires a research agenda that involves studying both HCI
					(Human-Computer Interaction) and software engineering research paths. Khora's research agenda
					thus implies working on two research axes:</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="main axes">
			<article class="axis-card">
				<span class="axis-number">1</span>

				<div class="axis-content">
					<p class="axis-label">Augmented Development Environment</p>
					<p class="main-text">
						By taking the perspective of developers, this axis will characterize and develop exploratory
						programming and propose novel approaches to build domain-specific and cutting-edge development
						environments (IDEs and digital twins) supporting domain-specific exploratory programming.
						Scientific contributions had worked on related topics, but they are mainly related to general-
						purpose languages (GPLs) and their general-purpose IDEs. Moreover, those contributions lack to
						work on easing the creation of domain-specific and highly interactive IDEs and digital twins.
					</p>
					<div class="keywords">
						<span>Exploratory programming</span>
						<span>Live programming</span>
						<span>DevX</span>
						<span>IDE</span>
						<span>Digital twin</span>
						<span>Interactive system engineering</span>
						<span>HCI</span>
						<span>V&V</span>
					</div>
				</div>
			</article>

			<article class="axis-card">
				<span class="axis-number">2</span>

				<div class="axis-content">
					<p class="axis-label">Augmented Code Analysis</p>
					<p class="main-text">
						While Axis 1 focuses on HCI engineering facets of exploratory programming, this second research axis
						focuses on underlying software engineering techniques to underpin this development mode. In particular,
						deterministic and explainable code analysis techniques will improve the precision of exploratory processes.
					</p>
					<div class="keywords">
						<span>Polyglot code analysis</span>
						<span>Scalable code analysis</span>
						<span>AI-based exploratory techniques</span>
						<span>Validity frame</span>
					</div>
				</div>
			</article>
		</section>

	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.team-name {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 7.5rem);
		line-height: 0.88;
		letter-spacing: -0.075em;
		font-weight: 650;
	}

	.axes {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
	}

	.axis-card {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 40px minmax(0, 1fr);
		align-items: start;
		padding-right: 20px;
	}

	.axis-number {
		grid-column: 1;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
	}

	.axis-label {
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.axis-content {
		grid-column: 2;
	}

	.axis-card + .axis-card {
		padding-left: 20px;
		border-left: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
	}

	.section-divider::before {
		content: "";
		display: block;
		width: 60%;
		height: 1px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		background: rgba(23, 24, 23, 0.12);
	}

</style>
